 6: /**
 7:  * Atlans (World 8 / `Object8`), the underwater map. `CreateObject`
 8:  * (ZzzObject.cpp:4718-4725) touches exactly one of the 41 types and
 9:  * `MoveObject` (:4005-4034) six more; `RenderObjectVisual` has no World 8
10:  * case at all. Almost everything those seven cases need is table data and
11:  * lives in `spec.ts` or in `common/meshAnimation.ts` - this file is the three
12:  * class assignments and the notes on what the original does here that we do
13:  * not.
14:  *
15:  * Type identities, from EncTerrain8.obj and the models: 0-2 seabed rock, 3-4
16:  * starfish, 5/6/21/26/31/33 seaweed, 7-10 decorative fish, 11-19 the Atlantis
17:  * palace, 20/29/30 stone, 22 bubble vent, 23 water plane, 24/25/27/28 kelp
18:  * (28 carries 91 bones), 32/34 coral lamps, 35-37 skeletons, 38 god-ray, 39
19:  * pose box, 40 anemone.
20:  *
21:  * **Not implemented, deliberately - the underwater layer.** Atlans is not
22:  * just a map with kelp on it; the original changes how the client behaves
23:  * while you are in it, and none of that is object work:
24:  *
25:  *  - **Swim locomotion.** `PLAYER_WALK_SWIM` (24) and `PLAYER_RUN_SWIM` (33)
26:  *    replace the walk/run clips for every character in World 8 (roadmap
27:  *    locomotion). The clips are already in the player GLBs and `playerPlaySpeed`
28:  *    already has their rates; what is missing is the map-conditional swap in
29:  *    the animation system.
30:  *  - **The terrain caustics pass.** `ZzzLodTerrain.cpp:1591` replaces layer-2
31:  *    tile 5 with a 32-frame `wt00..wt31` additive flipbook, which is what
32:  *    makes the seabed ripple. Terrain material work, not map work.
33:  *  - **Player head bubbles**, the boid fish shoals (`Object8/Fish02..09.glb`
34:  *    are placed by the boid code, not by EncTerrain8.obj - which is why they
35:  *    have no type numbers), and the 20 %-opacity shadows the original uses
36:  *    down here.
37:  *  - **No grass layer.** Atlans never renders one; the port has no grass
38:  *    layer to suppress yet.
39:  *
40:  * Music (`Music/atlans`) and the `Sound/aWater` ambient bed are wired
41:  * elsewhere.
42:  */
43: export async function createAtlans(world: World) {
44:   const terrain = world.terrain;
45:   if (!terrain) return;
46: 
47:   const tiles = terrain.MapTileObjects;
48: 
49:   // Atlans 22 (ZzzObject.cpp:4007-4012), ×845: hidden marker, bubbles on a
50:   // 4 s duty cycle. Effect-only (spec.ts) so the model never loads; the class
51:   // owns the timer and the emitter.
52:   tiles[22] = AtlansBubbleVentObject;
53: 
54:   // Atlans 39 (ZzzObject.cpp:4719-4723), ×4 - the "lean on the wall" pose
55:   // trigger, already mapped as `pose(true)` in libs/mu/restObjects.ts.
56:   //
57:   // `OperateBoxObject`, *not* `LeanBoxObject`: the Atlans case is
58:   // `CreateOperate(o); o->HiddenMesh = -2;` and nothing else. The
59:   // `Vector(40.f, 40.f, 160.f, o->BoundingBoxMax)` line that doubles the pick
60:   // box belongs to Lorencia's MODEL_POSE_BOX (:4585) and to Dungeon 60 /
61:   // Devias 91 / Market 67 - Atlans 39 keeps `CreateObject`'s default
62:   // `(-40,-40,0)…(40,40,80)` box (:4457-4494). loadMapIntoScene previously
63:   // registered the lean box here, which made these four triggers twice as
64:   // tall as the original's.
65:   tiles[39] = OperateBoxObject;
66: 
67:   // Atlans 40 (ZzzObject.cpp:4030-4034), ×86: the anemone, at a third speed.
68:   tiles[40] = AtlansAnemoneObject;
69: }
