 11:  *
 12:  * The map is 41 types (`Object01`..`Object41`, so `o->Type` 0..40) and 5215
 13:  * placed objects, of which the C++ touches six: 22, 23, 32, 34, 38 and 40 in
 14:  * `MoveObject` (ZzzObject.cpp:4005-4034) and 39 in `CreateObject` (:4719).
 15:  * `RenderObjectVisual` has no Atlans case at all - every swaying frond
 16:  * (5/6/21/24-28/31/33, up to 91 bones on 28) is baked BMD bone animation
 17:  * running at the default `o->Velocity = 0.16f`, so there is nothing to port
 18:  * for the kelp beyond loading it.
 19:  */
 20: 
 21: /**
 22:  * `MoveObject`, ZzzObject.cpp:4013-4034. Five types re-declare their
 23:  * `o->BlendMesh` every frame - an additive, unlit second pass over one mesh
 24:  * of the model:
 25:  *
 26:  *  - **23** (×10) the water plane, mesh 0 = `wt00.jpg`, the same caustics
 27:  *    sheet the terrain's layer-2 flipbook uses. Breathes on
 28:  *    `sin(WorldTime * 0.002) * 0.3 + 0.5` - table entry in `meshAnimation.ts`.
 29:  *  - **32** (×105) and **34** (×25), the glowing coral lamps. Both models are
 30:  *    two meshes, `wood05` (the coral body) and `wood052` (the glow shell), so
 31:  *    the blend index is 1 rather than 0; they pulse twice as fast and over
 32:  *    the full 0..1 range.
 33:  *  - **38** (×125) the god-ray / light shaft, one mesh of `light01.jpg`, held
 34:  *    at a constant `BlendMeshLight` - the original's breathing line is
 35:  *    commented out in the C++ (:4028) and is left out here too.
 36:  *  - **40** (×86) the anemone, one mesh of `ioi01.jpg`; see
 37:  *    `anemoneObject.ts` for the `o->Velocity = 0.05f` half of that case.
 38:  *
 39:  * Note `mapTileObject.ts` still carries three hand-written `Object8/*` cases
 40:  * from before this table existed (`Object39.glb` and `Object24.glb` forced to
 41:  * `ALPHA_ADD`, plus a `sin(t*2)` mesh-visibility fade on `Object24.glb` that
 42:  * is the type-23 `BlendMeshLight` done as alpha). They now duplicate - and,
 43:  * for type 23, override the material of - what this table and
 44:  * `meshAnimation.ts` do properly, and should be deleted with this wiring.
 45:  */
 46: export const ATLANS_BLEND_MESHES: Readonly<Record<number, number>> = {
 47:   23: 0,
 48:   32: 1,
 49:   34: 1,
 50:   38: 0,
 51:   40: 0,
