10:  * Devil Square (World10 / Object10) - the map entry: identity and the per-world data the
11:  * renderer, the terrain loader, the weather and the sound tables read.
12:  *
13:  * No `create`: every runtime behaviour of this map is table data (spec.ts) or
14:  * lives in another system; the notes below say what is and is not built.
15:  *
16:  * Devil Square (`WD_9DEVILSQUARE`, world 9 / `World10` + `Object10`).
17:  *
18:  * The whole map is the default `MapTileObject`: `CreateObject` and `MoveObject`
19:  * have no case for it, and its single `RenderObjectVisual` case - the rain
20:  * ripples on the 200 fence pillars - is documented and deliberately skipped in
21:  * `spec.ts`. What the square does at runtime is the *event*: the waves, the
22:  * timer and the rank table live in `events/devilSquare.ts`, and the rain in
23:  * the weather layer (the square is `outdoor` on its entry, per
24:  * `MoveLeaves`'s `MAX_LEAVES` budget for it).
25:  *
26:  * Sound: no `PlayWorldAmbientSounds` case, but `StopInactiveAmbientSounds`
27:  * (SceneManager.cpp:658) is the one place that spares the rain loop here, so
28:  * the `aRain` bed in `sound/ambientBeds.ts` is the original's, and there is no
29:  * music (`ManageBackgroundMusic` has no case; `devil_square_intro/outro.ogg`
30:  * are the event's stingers, not a map track).
31:  *
32:  * The four arenas share one terrain: DS1 at (44-87, 72-110), DS2 (118-152,
33:  * 72-110), DS3 (44-87, 140-184), DS4 (118-152, 140-184) - the server picks the
34:  * square by ticket level and sends the spawn with the warp. Offline lands in
35:  * DS1 at (133, 86).
36:  *
37:  * Squares 5-7 are OpenMU's map 32 (`WD_32DEVILSQUARE_5_7`). There is no
38:  * `World33` anywhere - the original's `LoadWorld` folds 32 into 9
39:  * (MapManager.cpp:1177) - so `assetWorldNum` (worldAssets.ts) draws map 32
40:  * from this same `World10`/`Object10`, and every per-world registry row is
41:  * spread over `DEVIL_SQUARE_WORLDS`.
42:  */
43: 
44: // ---- 1. data ---------------------------------------------------------------
45: 
46: // Squares 1-4 (map 9) and 5-7 (OpenMU map 32): `LoadWorld` folds 32 into 9
47: // (MapManager.cpp:1177) - one terrain, one object set, one entry.
